[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3438750922","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111965#issuecomment-3438750922","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111965","id":3438750922,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7M9yzK","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-23T19:23:46Z","updated_at":"2025-10-23T19:23:46Z","body":"There would probably need to be some way to create these without explicit ownership as there are times when we need to not do refcounting for safety, also in some low-level construction I'd say, though usually the cases where we want to avoid refcounting are when we already have a reference and we avoid referencing it again","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3438750922/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3438756101","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111965#issuecomment-3438756101","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111965","id":3438756101,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7M90EF","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-23T19:25:16Z","updated_at":"2025-10-23T19:25:16Z","body":"To me it looks like the problem is that some people used RefCounted wrong. You should either not use it with `memnew()`, or wrap that in Ref (AFAIK `Ref<Type>(memnew(Type))` ensures proper ownership). Using `instantiate()` is more or less established in the codebase, so this PR only adds another available syntax for creating RefCounted objects. Instead of doing that, we could prevent the wrong usage.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3438756101/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3438761786","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111965#issuecomment-3438761786","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111965","id":3438761786,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7M91c6","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-23T19:26:43Z","updated_at":"2025-10-23T19:32:13Z","body":"> There would probably need to be some way to create these without explicit ownership as there are times when we need to not do refcounting for safety, also in some low-level construction I'd say, though usually the cases where we want to avoid refcounting are when we already have a reference and we avoid referencing it again\r\n\r\nCould you provide an example? Usually the only reason to avoid ref counting is performance, and you can still pass `RefCounted` objects around by reference.\r\n\r\n> To me it looks like the problem is that some people used RefCounted wrong.\r\n\r\nThis is part of the problem, but just using `.instantiate()` wouldn't solve the second problem from the OP.\r\n\r\n> You should either not use it with memnew(), or wrap that in Ref (AFAIK Ref<Type>(memnew(Type)) ensures proper ownership). Using instantiate() is more or less established in the codebase, so this PR only adds another available syntax for creating RefCounted objects. \r\n\r\nThis PR basically enforces the `Ref<Type>(memnew(Type))` style for callers with `memnew`. It doesn't introduce new syntax.\r\n\r\n> Instead of doing that, we could prevent the wrong usage.\r\n\r\nYea, disallowing `memnew` for all `RefCounted` objects could be done as well, in the context of this PR. It's just a matter of stylistic preference whether we want `memnew` for all objects or just non-refcounted ones.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3438761786/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3438783165","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111965#issuecomment-3438783165","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111965","id":3438783165,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7M96q9","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-23T19:32:16Z","updated_at":"2025-10-23T19:32:16Z","body":"> Could you provide an example? Usually the only reason to avoid ref counting is performance, and you can still pass `RefCounted` objects around by reference.\r\n\r\nI can't remember where it was currently, but and I think that was related to creating `Ref` where there already was ownership, but it had to do with dangling copies and extending ownership in some contexts, but it might not be directly relevant, but might be cases where the choice to use a raw pointer is not an error\r\n\r\n> This PR basically enforces the `Ref<Type>(memnew(Type))` style for callers with `memnew`.\r\n\r\nBut that's establishing a *different* style than what is established","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3438783165/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3438794234","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111965#issuecomment-3438794234","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111965","id":3438794234,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7M99X6","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-23T19:35:00Z","updated_at":"2025-10-23T19:35:44Z","body":"> This PR basically enforces the Ref<Type>(memnew(Type)) style for callers with memnew. It doesn't introduce new syntax.\r\n\r\nI meant \"new syntax\" for RefCounted objects. After this PR you can do `Ref<Type> var = memnew(Type)`, which wasn't possible before.\r\n\r\n> This is part of the problem, but just using .instantiate() wouldn't solve the second problem from the OP.\r\n\r\nRight, so I guess that would justify this change.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3438794234/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3438805541","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111965#issuecomment-3438805541","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111965","id":3438805541,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7M-AIl","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-23T19:37:15Z","updated_at":"2025-10-23T19:37:15Z","body":"> After this PR you can do `Ref<Type> var = memnew(Type)`, which wasn't possible before.\r\n\r\nThat is fully code wise possible currently? You don't have to do `Ref<Type> var = Ref<Type>(memnew(Type))`","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3438805541/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3438811617","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111965#issuecomment-3438811617","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111965","id":3438811617,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7M-Bnh","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-23T19:38:35Z","updated_at":"2025-10-23T19:39:18Z","body":"> I can't remember where it was currently, but and I think that was related to creating `Ref` where there already was ownership, but it had to do with dangling copies and extending ownership in some contexts, but it might not be directly relevant, but might be cases where the choice to use a raw pointer is not an error\r\n\r\nI think using _any_ refcounted object without a primary owner is an error. Passing it around via pointer is fine, but owning one without it is always unsafe, because anyone you pass it to can destroy your object (even by accident).\r\n\r\n> > This PR basically enforces the `Ref<Type>(memnew(Type))` style for callers with `memnew`.\r\n> \r\n> But that's establishing a _different_ style than what is established\r\n\r\nThat's true. I have some problems with `.instantiate()`, but not enough to warrant churning the whole codebase to change it. It's a good argument for going with the \"forbid\" route instead.\r\n\r\n> > This PR basically enforces the Ref(memnew(Type)) style for callers with memnew. It doesn't introduce new syntax.\r\n> \r\n> I meant \"new syntax\" for RefCounted objects. After this PR you can do `Ref<Type> var = memnew(Type)`, which wasn't possible before.\r\n\r\nThis is already possible in `master`. `Ref` has an implicit conversion from `T *`.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3438811617/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3438835363","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111965#issuecomment-3438835363","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111965","id":3438835363,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7M-Haj","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-23T19:44:57Z","updated_at":"2025-10-23T19:44:57Z","body":"One potential issue I would see is that this could hide incorrect code, it *should* be the case that:\r\n```cpp\r\nRef<T1> t1 = memnew(T2);\r\n```\r\nFails when `T2` is not derived from `T1`, but with this change it would be a silent empty `Ref`, though I haven't tested if the former actually does fail but it should\r\n\r\nThough ultimately we don't want `Ref<T> t = memnew(T);` except where it's actually necessary, like when constructing a derived type, though those would usually be cases where it's not a declaration but later, like:\r\n```cpp\r\nRef<Texture2D> tex;\r\n...\r\ntex = memnew(ImageTexture(...));\r\n```","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3438835363/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3438851553","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111965#issuecomment-3438851553","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111965","id":3438851553,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7M-LXh","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-23T19:48:27Z","updated_at":"2025-10-23T20:32:20Z","body":"> One potential issue I would see is that this could hide incorrect code, it _should_ be the case that:\r\n> \r\n> ```c++\r\n> Ref<T1> t1 = memnew(T2);\r\n> ```\r\n> Fails when `T2` is not derived from `T1`, but with this change it would be a silent empty `Ref`, though I haven't tested if the former actually does fail but it should\r\n\r\nThat's a good point. This was also previously a problem (when using the `memnew` syntax). But it can be easily resolved to fail at compile time. I'll make a note to add a pull request for that.\r\nEdit: #111967 ","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3438851553/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3438857381","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111965#issuecomment-3438857381","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111965","id":3438857381,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7M-Myl","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-23T19:50:04Z","updated_at":"2025-10-23T20:02:10Z","body":"It shouldn't have been a problem as it should fail to compiletime right now, I can't test it right now but it should as `T2 *` can't be cast to `T1 *` unless `T2` is `T1` or a derived type\r\n\r\nSo this would be a change in this PR, so I'd say a check for this at compile time should be in this PR \r\n\r\nI'd test just with:\r\n```cpp\r\nRef<Texture3D> r = memnew(ImageTexture2D(...));\r\n```\r\n\r\nEdit: There isn't really any way I can see that this can be guarded against, not sure how we can resolve that at compile time, as it's just `Ref<T> t = Ref<T2>(memnew(T2));` so the problem isn't solvable as far as I can tell\r\n\r\nTo clarify the problem:\r\n\r\nThis fails (and should fail to make it clear to the user they're doing something wrong):\r\n```cpp\r\nRef<Texture2D> t = memnew(Texture3D);\r\n```\r\nBut this *doesn't* (as conversion is fully permitted between `Ref`):\r\n```cpp\r\nRef<Texture3D> t3 = memnew(Texture3D);\r\nRef<Texture2D> t = t3;\r\n```\r\nThe result will be that `t` is empty though\r\n\r\nWith this change the first case will not fail at compile time, it will just yield an empty result, making this very hard to diagnose if you, for example, accidentally picked the wrong type when doing something","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3438857381/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3438877007","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111965#issuecomment-3438877007","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111965","id":3438877007,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7M-RlP","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-23T19:54:24Z","updated_at":"2025-10-23T19:54:24Z","body":"If we want to continue to allow code like this (from [ATS' comment](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111965#issuecomment-3438835363) above):\r\n\r\n> ```c++\r\n> Ref<Texture2D> tex;\r\n> ...\r\n> tex = memnew(ImageTexture(...));\r\n> ```\r\n\r\nThen I think we need the changes in this PR. Because without this PR, in code like that it's still possible for a class to accidentally delete itself during `NOTIFICATION_POSTINITIALIZE`, which is what this is aiming to fix.\r\n\r\nMaybe some of the push back here can be addressed by changing the `memnew()` conversions that @Ivorforce did into `.instantiate()` where possible?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3438877007/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3868481748","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111965#issuecomment-3868481748","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111965","id":3868481748,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7mlFjU","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-08T22:49:23Z","updated_at":"2026-02-08T22:49:23Z","body":"I've updated the PR to use `.instantiate()` instead of `memnew` where possible. I still do not agree that `.instantiate()` is the better choice over `memnew`, but this is not in scope of this PR to challenge.\r\n\r\nI've also rebased, things build again. Hoping to get this PR merged for early 4.7 :)","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3868481748/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4093185951","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111965#issuecomment-4093185951","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111965","id":4093185951,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7z-Q-f","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://git